      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6164ea6864fa800d425cecbb|full_name}: all bones (apart from physbones) are networked as IK. as far as im aware of, there is no real reason as to why we couldnt directly drive a bones rotation bypassing parameters - it'd also use less bandwidth on the network by simply networking less things!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
